WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.734
New attacks on

00:00:00.734 --> 00:00:01.468
the capital, Kyiv,

00:00:01.468 --> 00:00:03.169
after weeks of relative calm.

00:00:03.169 --> 00:00:04.571
Ukraine's armed forces say

00:00:04.571 --> 00:00:05.338
Russia unleashed,

00:00:05.338 --> 00:00:08.108
at least unleashed at least 12 drones,

00:00:08.541 --> 00:00:10.410
but it says most were destroyed

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:12.679
and there were no casualties or damage.

00:00:13.046 --> 00:00:14.214
This as Russian state

00:00:14.214 --> 00:00:14.914
media says,

00:00:14.914 --> 00:00:15.882
a large blast

00:00:15.882 --> 00:00:18.118
in the Russian city of Belgorod

00:00:18.184 --> 00:00:20.186
close to the Ukrainian border was caused

00:00:20.186 --> 00:00:21.321
by an emergency

00:00:21.321 --> 00:00:23.056
release of an air ordnance

00:00:23.056 --> 00:00:25.458
from a Russian warplane.

00:00:25.458 --> 00:00:26.860
There was significant damage.

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:27.827
At least one analyst

00:00:27.827 --> 00:00:30.330
described the scenario as odd.

00:00:30.363 --> 00:00:31.931
Let's bring in Ben Wedeman.

00:00:31.931 --> 00:00:32.999
He joins me from Kiev.

00:00:32.999 --> 00:00:35.335
It does sound rather odd

00:00:36.603 --> 00:00:37.470
right?

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:38.571
Odd indeed.

00:00:38.571 --> 00:00:41.408
This happened at about 10:15 o'clock

00:00:41.941 --> 00:00:44.444
last night local time, wherein

00:00:44.611 --> 00:00:47.747
some 35 twin engine fighter bomber

00:00:48.214 --> 00:00:49.516
dropped a bomb.

00:00:49.516 --> 00:00:50.050
I mean,

00:00:50.216 --> 00:00:51.751
the use of this emergency

00:00:51.751 --> 00:00:53.787
release of an airborne of an air

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:55.455
ordnance, they dropped a bomb

00:00:55.455 --> 00:00:56.823
on a busy street

00:00:56.823 --> 00:00:59.592
in the middle of this city of 400,000

00:01:00.093 --> 00:01:00.627
people.

00:01:00.627 --> 00:01:03.396
Now we saw on CCTV that

00:01:04.164 --> 00:01:06.399
the hit sort of on a sidewalk

00:01:06.399 --> 00:01:08.401
by the side of this busy

00:01:08.401 --> 00:01:11.304
road causing one car to fly up

00:01:11.805 --> 00:01:12.605
into the air.

00:01:12.605 --> 00:01:14.874
Now according to the mayor of Belgorod,

00:01:14.874 --> 00:01:17.777
two people were injured in this incident.

00:01:17.811 --> 00:01:19.312
Now it is odd

00:01:19.312 --> 00:01:21.381
that this would happen

00:01:21.381 --> 00:01:22.248
in the middle of the town.

00:01:22.248 --> 00:01:23.583
Normally if

00:01:23.583 --> 00:01:26.386
a pilot is experiencing problems,

00:01:26.719 --> 00:01:29.856
if he has to drop his bomb by mistake,

00:01:29.856 --> 00:01:32.325
but because of technical difficulties,

00:01:32.559 --> 00:01:33.660
he would do it in

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:35.462
an unpopular shaded area,

00:01:35.462 --> 00:01:37.964
not in the middle of a city.

00:01:37.964 --> 00:01:40.767
No.
Belgorod is only 40 kilometers

00:01:41.301 --> 00:01:43.269
from the border with Ukraine

00:01:43.269 --> 00:01:45.305
and on more than one occasion,

00:01:45.305 --> 00:01:47.006
the Ukrainians have fired back

00:01:47.006 --> 00:01:48.641
in the direction of that city,

00:01:48.641 --> 00:01:49.275
I think

00:01:49.275 --> 00:01:50.577
in the early months,

00:01:50.577 --> 00:01:52.445
weeks of the war, actually.

00:01:52.445 --> 00:01:54.481
A Ukrainian helicopter

00:01:54.481 --> 00:01:56.816
conducted a strike on the city.

00:01:57.083 --> 00:01:59.552
I think sometimes it's hit by Ukrainian

00:02:00.086 --> 00:02:01.054
drones as well.

00:02:01.054 --> 00:02:04.257
But this incident certainly will jog

00:02:04.257 --> 00:02:05.325
it will be jarring

00:02:05.325 --> 00:02:07.227
to many of the residents

00:02:07.227 --> 00:02:08.928
of that city Max.

00:02:08.928 --> 00:02:10.597
Okay, Ben, thank you.

00:02:10.597 --> 00:02:10.997
The U.S.

00:02:10.997 --> 00:02:11.598
says Western

00:02:11.598 --> 00:02:14.667
allies have now provided $55 billion

00:02:14.667 --> 00:02:16.536
in security assistance to Ukraine

00:02:16.536 --> 00:02:17.203
and are promising

00:02:17.203 --> 00:02:18.905
to build on their progress.

00:02:18.905 --> 00:02:19.506
The US defense

00:02:19.506 --> 00:02:21.207
secretary spoke at the Ukraine Defense

00:02:21.207 --> 00:02:22.208
Contact Group

00:02:22.208 --> 00:02:23.676
meeting in Ramstein, Germany,

00:02:23.676 --> 00:02:24.644
where he had

00:02:24.644 --> 00:02:26.412
where he said America rejects

00:02:26.412 --> 00:02:28.715
Vladimir Putin's view of the world.

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:32.819
All of
us have come together

00:02:32.819 --> 00:02:34.921
to stand up for Ukraine

00:02:34.921 --> 00:02:35.788
and for a world

00:02:35.788 --> 00:02:38.825
based on rules and rights.

00:02:39.492 --> 00:02:42.529
We reject Putin's grim vision of a world

00:02:42.529 --> 00:02:44.130
where tyrants get to assault

00:02:44.130 --> 00:02:46.232
their peaceful neighbors

00:02:46.332 --> 00:02:49.169
and try to impose self self-declare

00:02:49.335 --> 00:02:52.038
spheres of influence at gunpoint.

00:02:53.506 --> 00:02:54.841
Also speaking from Rammstein,

00:02:54.841 --> 00:02:55.942
the head of NATO's,

00:02:55.942 --> 00:02:57.944
who said the alliance remains committed

00:02:57.944 --> 00:03:01.681
to Ukraine's eventual membership.

00:03:01.681 --> 00:03:03.416
All Needle allies have agreed

00:03:03.416 --> 00:03:07.320
that Ukraine will become a NATO member,

00:03:08.955 --> 00:03:11.591
but the main focus now is, of course, on

00:03:12.759 --> 00:03:15.895
on how to ensure that Ukraine prevails.

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:19.232
Sebastian here with more.

00:03:19.232 --> 00:03:20.800
And Ukraine always wants more than

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:21.701
what is being promised.

00:03:21.701 --> 00:03:22.202
Would you expect

00:03:22.202 --> 00:03:23.369
they're going to get today?

00:03:23.369 --> 00:03:24.571
Well, so we know so far

00:03:24.571 --> 00:03:25.772
that Alexi Reznik

00:03:25.772 --> 00:03:26.706
of who is the defense

00:03:26.706 --> 00:03:28.174
minister, has had a bilateral meeting

00:03:28.174 --> 00:03:29.609
with the U.S.

00:03:29.609 --> 00:03:30.643
defense secretary,

00:03:30.643 --> 00:03:31.811
Lloyd Austin, who you just saw there.

00:03:31.811 --> 00:03:32.979
He said it was fruitful.

00:03:32.979 --> 00:03:34.781
We don't know exactly

00:03:34.781 --> 00:03:36.449
what kind of promises were made.

00:03:36.449 --> 00:03:37.817
The US went into this meeting

00:03:37.817 --> 00:03:39.285
saying there were three key issues

00:03:39.285 --> 00:03:40.920
air defense, ammunition

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:42.188
and what they call enablers,

00:03:42.188 --> 00:03:43.289
which are things that sort of help

00:03:43.289 --> 00:03:44.123
the overall mission,

00:03:44.123 --> 00:03:45.091
things like heavy duty

00:03:45.091 --> 00:03:47.427
trucks and stuff to transport equipment.

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:49.529
The Ukrainian side went into it

00:03:49.529 --> 00:03:51.297
specifically asking for NATO's

00:03:51.297 --> 00:03:52.232
standard fighter jet.

00:03:52.232 --> 00:03:52.932
So it would seem that

00:03:52.932 --> 00:03:54.033
there is some daylight.

00:03:54.033 --> 00:03:55.201
But of course, they are

00:03:55.201 --> 00:03:55.735
very clear

00:03:55.735 --> 00:03:56.936
rhetorically exactly

00:03:56.936 --> 00:03:57.837
that the NATO's side

00:03:57.837 --> 00:03:58.771
that they are in this

00:03:58.771 --> 00:03:59.372
for the long haul,

00:03:59.372 --> 00:04:00.607
that they stand with Ukraine

00:04:00.607 --> 00:04:01.307
are going to continue

00:04:01.307 --> 00:04:02.775
to tailor their response

00:04:02.775 --> 00:04:04.143
to the situation on the battlefield.

00:04:04.143 --> 00:04:06.446
I think the other elephant in the room,

00:04:06.446 --> 00:04:07.046
clearly at this

00:04:07.046 --> 00:04:09.215
meeting is the issue of those Pentagon

00:04:09.215 --> 00:04:11.284
leaks, how that happened.

00:04:11.284 --> 00:04:11.718
The U.S.

00:04:11.718 --> 00:04:12.785
trying to smooth things

00:04:12.785 --> 00:04:14.220
over a little bit with its allies.

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:14.587
Take a listen

00:04:14.587 --> 00:04:15.588
to what Lloyd Austin had to say

00:04:15.588 --> 00:04:16.088
about that.

00:04:17.523 --> 00:04:17.890
As I've

00:04:17.890 --> 00:04:18.625
discussed this

00:04:18.625 --> 00:04:20.827
issue with our allies and partners,

00:04:22.028 --> 00:04:24.631
I've been struck by your solidarity

00:04:25.498 --> 00:04:26.499
and your commitment

00:04:26.499 --> 00:04:28.801
to reject efforts to divide us.

00:04:30.169 --> 00:04:32.839
And we will not let anything

00:04:32.839 --> 00:04:35.475
fracture our unity

00:04:36.175 --> 00:04:37.143
So it would seem

00:04:37.143 --> 00:04:39.345
that's not just a message to

00:04:39.345 --> 00:04:40.513
his allies in the room,

00:04:40.513 --> 00:04:41.781
but also to Moscow

00:04:41.781 --> 00:04:43.383
that NATO is standing firm

00:04:43.383 --> 00:04:44.517
in its support for Ukraine.

00:04:44.517 --> 00:04:45.718
We did get come in in response

00:04:45.718 --> 00:04:46.519
not to that,

00:04:46.519 --> 00:04:47.487
but to the comments

00:04:47.487 --> 00:04:48.888
from the NATO's secretary general

00:04:48.888 --> 00:04:49.889
saying that the alliance

00:04:49.889 --> 00:04:51.324
is essentially united on the view

00:04:51.324 --> 00:04:52.025
that Ukraine

00:04:52.025 --> 00:04:53.793
should join the Kremlin, saying

00:04:53.793 --> 00:04:54.761
that Neato continues

00:04:54.761 --> 00:04:56.229
to show its aggressive nature.

00:04:56.229 --> 00:04:56.629
They said

00:04:56.629 --> 00:04:58.464
we're dealing with a dangerous bloc

00:04:58.464 --> 00:05:00.500
that counts our country as an enemy.

00:05:00.500 --> 00:05:01.601
Okay, Clare, thank you.

